# What `railway up` must not upload.
#
# Railway falls back to .gitignore when this file is absent, which already
# covers the env files — but "already covered by something else" is a poor
# reason to leave secrets depending on an inherited default. The Docker build
# context has its own explicit list in .dockerignore for the same reason.

# Secrets. .env and .env.docker hold a real ENCRYPTION_KEY and API keys; the
# deployed services get their configuration from Railway variables instead.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.production.example
!.env.docker.example

# Rebuilt inside the image.
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Local state and editor noise.
.git
.railway
.claude
.vscode
.idea
*.log
